IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain

-- g2-nouns.l4: the nouns that group G2 (Articles 3 to 7 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014) adds to domain.l4.
-- It holds only DECLAREs: no rules and no directives.  domain.l4 is read-only for this group, so a noun that G2 needs and domain.l4 lacks is declared here as a
-- local stand-in, and FRAGMENT-G2.md lists it as a "nouns request" for the INTEGRATOR.
-- The four Article modules of the group import this module; this module imports only prelude, daydate and domain.
-- The record `Interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` is the group's one record of forks (BRIEF: "Forks: the R4 shape"); every public decision of the group that depends on a reading takes it.

§ `G2 nouns: Articles 3 to 7`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 1. What is done: the acts of the regulative rules of Articles 3 to 7
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- The subjects on which the Commissioner publishes guidance.  Article 4(1)(d) speaks of guidance on the operation of the Law, "including guidance on the duties of governors and
-- guidance on the charity test under Article 5(4)"; Article 5(4) speaks of guidance on the determination of whether an entity meets the charity test; Article 7(4) adds that the
-- guidance published under Article 5(4) must in particular give guidance on the determination of public benefit.
DECLARE `Subject of the Commissioner's guidance` IS ONE OF
    `the operation of the Law, including the duties of governors and the charity test`
    `the determination of whether an entity meets the charity test`
    `the determination of whether an entity provides or intends to provide public benefit`

-- The acts that the regulative rules of Articles 3 to 7 are about, named for what is done and not for the Article that requires it.
-- Each constructor carries its performer as its FIRST field of type `Legal actor` (domain.l4), which is how L4 checks that a PARTY performs only its own acts.
DECLARE `Act under Articles 3 to 7` IS ONE OF
    `publish and maintain guidance`
        HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
            on IS A `Subject of the Commissioner's guidance`
    `seek to act in a way that protects public trust and confidence in registered charities and is proportionate`
        HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `do something that is calculated to facilitate, or is conducive or incidental to, the performance of a function`
        HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `provide information to the public about the system of registration of charities`
        HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `advise the Minister about charities in Jersey and further regulation of them`
        HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `assist an equivalent body outside Jersey in the performance of its functions`
        HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `have regard to the guidance`
        HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `have regard to how benefit to members or other persons (other than as members of the public) and disbenefit to the public compare with benefit to the public`
        HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `have regard to whether any condition on obtaining a benefit provided to a section of the public only, including a charge or fee, is unduly restrictive`
        HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `presume a particular charitable purpose to be for the public benefit`
        HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `treat one particular natural person or a group of identified natural persons as a section of the public`
        HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `treat an entity that benefits only one natural person or a group of identified natural persons as providing public benefit`
        HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `make an Order disapplying the bar on control by a Minister, a member of the States Assembly or an equivalent`
        HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `consult`
        HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
            `persons appearing to the Commissioner to be representative of charities or bodies with charitable purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
            `the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
            `such other persons as the Commissioner considers appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `publish a report on the views on the consultation and the reasons for the decision on the guidance`
        HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `provide to the Minister a copy of the issued or amended guidance and the report`
        HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `lay a copy of the guidance and report before the States`
        HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `make Regulations adding sub-paragraphs to the list of charitable purposes or to its explanations`
        HAS by IS A `Legal actor`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 2. Article 4(4): how the Commissioner acted, limb by limb
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- One limb of the standard of conduct in Article 4(4), as the Commissioner's own record of it.  "So far appears to him or her to be reasonably practicable" is the Commissioner's
-- opinion, so it is an input; whether the Commissioner then sought to act in that way is a fact.
DECLARE `A limb of the standard of conduct in Article 4(4)`
    HAS `it appeared to the Commissioner to be reasonably practicable to act in that way` IS A BOOLEAN
        `the Commissioner sought to act in that way` IS A BOOLEAN

-- The five limbs of Article 4(4)(a) and (b): protects public trust and confidence in registered charities; is compatible with the encouragement of all forms of charitable giving;
-- is compatible with the encouragement of voluntary participation in the work of registered charities; is proportionate as to the burdens imposed on registered charities; supports
-- the development of registered charities.
DECLARE `How the Commissioner acted in performing a function`
    HAS `protects public trust and confidence in registered charities` IS A `A limb of the standard of conduct in Article 4(4)`
        `is compatible with the encouragement of all forms of charitable giving` IS A `A limb of the standard of conduct in Article 4(4)`
        `is compatible with the encouragement of voluntary participation in the work of registered charities` IS A `A limb of the standard of conduct in Article 4(4)`
        `is proportionate as to the burdens imposed on registered charities` IS A `A limb of the standard of conduct in Article 4(4)`
        `supports the development of registered charities` IS A `A limb of the standard of conduct in Article 4(4)`

-- The three examples that Article 4(3) lists.
DECLARE `Example listed in Article 4(3)` IS ONE OF
    `providing information to the public about the system of registration of charities`
    `advising the Minister about charities in Jersey and further regulation of them`
    `assisting an equivalent body outside Jersey in the performance of its functions`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 3. Article 5(2): what the constitution expressly permits
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- The persons that Article 5(2)(a) to (c) names.  For "a Minister" the constructor carries, if the Minister holds the office that Article 1 calls "the Minister" in some text of the Law
-- (the Chief Minister, the Minister for External Relations, the Minister for External Relations and Financial Services), that office; NOTHING for any other ministerial office
-- (the Minister for Health, say).  Only the second reading of fork F2.3 reads the office.
DECLARE `Person named in Article 5(2)` IS ONE OF
    `a Minister`
        HAS `the office that Article 1 calls the Minister, if the Minister holds it` IS A MAYBE `Office of the Minister`
    `a member of the States Assembly`
    `any equivalent of a Minister or of a member of the States Assembly in another jurisdiction`

-- The two things Article 5(2) says a constitution may expressly permit.
DECLARE `What a constitution expressly permits` IS ONE OF
    `the activities of the entity to be directed or otherwise controlled by`
    `any of the governors of the entity to be`

-- One permission found in the text of an entity's constitution.  `acting in that capacity` records whether the permitted person is to act as a Minister, a member or an equivalent
-- (ex officio or in that office), which fork F2.2 asks about.
DECLARE `Permission that a constitution expressly makes`
    HAS `what the constitution expressly permits` IS A `What a constitution expressly permits`
        `the person permitted` IS A `Person named in Article 5(2)`
        `acting in that capacity` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Everything Article 5(2) reads about the constitution: the permissions of the kinds above that its text expressly makes.  An empty list means that it makes none.
DECLARE `Facts about the constitution under Article 5(2)`
    HAS `permissions that the constitution expressly makes` IS A LIST OF `Permission that a constitution expressly makes`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 4. Article 6: the facts about a purpose that the clarifications in Article 6(2) read
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- domain.l4 gives a Purpose its head (a judgement) and three flags.  Article 6(2) narrows head (h) and head (i) and extends heads (d), (f) and (n), and head (l) joins two ideas with
-- "and", so those clauses need facts that `Purpose` does not carry.  They are declared here as a stand-in (nouns request N1 of FRAGMENT-G2.md).
-- A MAYBE field is read only when the head makes it relevant; NOTHING says "not stated".
-- The tenth field, the object of 6(1)(i), was added after independent testing (src:176: "with the object of improving the conditions of life for the persons for whom the facilities or
-- activities are primarily intended"); it comes last so that the first nine keep their positions, and a JSON row that leaves it out takes NOTHING.
DECLARE `Facts about a purpose under Article 6`
    HAS `the purpose is the prevention or relief of sickness, disease or human suffering` IS A BOOLEAN
        `the purpose is rural or urban regeneration` IS A BOOLEAN
        `the purpose is the promotion of civic responsibility, volunteering, the voluntary sector or the effectiveness or efficiency of registered charities` IS A BOOLEAN
        `the sport involves physical skill and exertion` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
        `the facilities or activities are primarily intended for persons who have need of them by reason of their age, ill-health, disability, financial hardship or other disadvantage` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
        `the facilities or activities are available to members of the public at large or to male or female members of the public at large` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
        `the purpose is relief of those in need by reason of age, ill-health, disability, financial hardship or other disadvantage, given by the provision of accommodation or care` IS A BOOLEAN
        `the purpose promotes equality` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
        `the purpose promotes diversity` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
        `the facilities or activities have the object of improving the conditions of life for the persons for whom they are primarily intended` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN TYPICALLY NOTHING

-- A purpose together with the facts that Article 6 reads about it.
DECLARE `Purpose with the facts Article 6 reads`
    HAS purpose IS A Purpose
        facts IS A `Facts about a purpose under Article 6`

-- The content of Regulations that the States propose to make under Article 6(3), as far as Article 6(3) and (4) read it.
DECLARE `Content of Regulations under Article 6(3)`
    HAS `adds sub-paragraphs to paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
        `adds sub-paragraphs to paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
        `the sub-paragraphs added to paragraph (2) make explanatory provision in relation to sub-paragraphs added to paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
        `amends or restricts the effect of any of paragraphs (1)(a) to (p) and (2)(a) to (f)` IS A BOOLEAN
        `alters the effect of paragraph (5)` IS A BOOLEAN

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 5. Article 7: a determination of public benefit
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- What a person who determined whether an entity provides, or intends to provide, public benefit found and did.  Article 7(1) binds the Commissioner, the tribunal and the court to
-- paragraphs (2) and (3); Article 5(5) binds any person to have regard to the guidance.  "To a reasonable degree" is the finding itself and is not computed.
DECLARE `Determination of public benefit`
    HAS `who made the determination` IS A `Legal actor`
        `the determination finds that the entity provides public benefit in Jersey or elsewhere to a reasonable degree` IS A BOOLEAN
        `the determination finds that the entity intends to provide public benefit in Jersey or elsewhere to a reasonable degree` IS A BOOLEAN
        `regard was had to the guidance published under Article 5(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
        `regard was had to how benefit gained or likely to be gained by members of the entity or other persons (other than as members of the public), and disbenefit incurred or likely to be incurred by the public, compare with the benefit gained or likely to be gained by the public` IS A BOOLEAN
        `benefit is, or is likely to be, provided to a section of the public only` IS A BOOLEAN
        `regard was had to whether any condition on obtaining the benefit, including any charge or fee, is unduly restrictive` IS A BOOLEAN
        `a particular charitable purpose was presumed to be for the public benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
        `the entity benefits only one particular natural person or a group of identified natural persons` IS A BOOLEAN
        `one particular natural person or a group of identified natural persons was treated as a section of the public` IS A BOOLEAN

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 6. Article 5: which limb decides the charity test
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- The first limb of the charity test, taken in the order the text states them (5(1)(a), 5(1)(b), then 5(2) for an entity that otherwise meets the test), that the entity does not meet.
DECLARE `Limb of the charity test that decides it` IS ONE OF
    `none: the entity meets the charity test`
    `Article 5(1)(a) is not met: a purpose is neither a charitable purpose nor purely ancillary or incidental to one`
        HAS `the purposes that are neither` IS A LIST OF Purpose
    `Article 5(1)(a) is not met: the entity has no charitable purpose`
    `Article 5(1)(b) is not met: the entity does not provide public benefit to a reasonable degree`
    `Article 5(2) bars an entity that otherwise meets the charity test`
    `Article 5(1) does not apply: the body is not an entity within Article 2(1)`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 7. The forks of Articles 3 to 7 (the R4 shape): one enumeration per fork point, all of them fields of one record
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- F2.1.  Article 5(1)(a): "all of its purposes are (i) charitable purposes, or (ii) purposes that are purely ancillary or incidental to any of its charitable purposes".
DECLARE `How the purposes of an entity are tested in Article 5(1)(a)` IS ONE OF
    `at least one charitable purpose is required, and an ancillary purpose counts only beside one`
    `an entity with no purposes satisfies the test vacuously`
    `purely ancillary purposes satisfy the test without any charitable purpose`

-- F2.2.  Article 5(2): "acting in that capacity".
DECLARE `How "acting in that capacity" qualifies the persons named in Article 5(2)` IS ONE OF
    `the person must be permitted to act as a Minister, a member of the States Assembly or an equivalent`
    `any such person is caught however the person is to act`

-- F2.3.  Article 5(2)(a): "a Minister", against Article 1: "Minister" means the Chief Minister (in the text of 2 October 2026).
DECLARE `What "a Minister" means in Article 5(2)(a)` IS ONE OF
    `any Minister of the Government of Jersey`
    `only the Minister, as Article 1 defines the term in the text in force`

-- F2.4.  Article 5(7) "within a reasonable time" and Article 5(8) "as soon as practicable".
DECLARE `How a standard of promptness in Articles 5(7) and 5(8) is measured` IS ONE OF
    `by an input judgement that the time taken was reasonable or practicable`
    `by a number of days counted from the event`

-- F2.5.  Article 6(2)(f), Article 6(1)(c), Article 6(1)(p).
DECLARE `Which head a purpose of advancing a philosophical belief falls within` IS ONE OF
    `paragraph (1)(p), by the analogy that Article 6(2)(f) states`
    `paragraph (1)(c), as if the analogy made it a purpose of advancing religion`

-- F2.6.  The counting convention of a period measured in days from an event (Articles 5(7) and 5(8) under the second reading of F2.4).
DECLARE `How the days of a period measured from an event are counted` IS ONE OF
    `the day of the event is not counted, so the day after it is the first day`
    `the day of the event is the first day`

-- F2.7.  Article 5(6): "Before issuing or amending guidance" (a backward period: the boundary day).
DECLARE `How "before issuing or amending guidance" in Article 5(6) is read` IS ONE OF
    `the consultation and the report must fall on an earlier day than the day the guidance is issued or amended`
    `the consultation and the report may fall on the day the guidance is issued or amended`

-- F2.8.  Article 4(3): "may in particular, without prejudice to the generality of his or her powers".
DECLARE `Whether the examples in Article 4(3) add to Article 4(2)` IS ONE OF
    `the examples illustrate Article 4(2) and are bound by its conditions`
    `each example is a power in its own right`

-- F2.9.  Article 4(4): "so far appears to him or her to be reasonably practicable".
DECLARE `How "so far as reasonably practicable" qualifies the standard of conduct in Article 4(4)` IS ONE OF
    `each limb binds so far as it appeared reasonably practicable`
    `the standard binds only if it appeared reasonably practicable to act in the whole way`

-- F2.10.  Articles 5(5), 7(2) and 7(3) bind the maker of a determination of public benefit; the Law does not say what follows from a breach.
DECLARE `What follows from a determination of public benefit made in breach of the duties on its maker` IS ONE OF
    `the determination does not answer the question`
    `the finding of the determination stands`
    `the entity is treated as not providing public benefit`

-- F2.11.  Article 6(1)(l): "the promotion of equality and diversity".
DECLARE `How "equality and diversity" in Article 6(1)(l) is read` IS ONE OF
    `a purpose must promote both equality and diversity`
    `a purpose that promotes either equality or diversity suffices`

-- F2.12.  Article 5(6): "Before issuing or amending guidance" and Article 5(7), 5(8): which guidance do Articles 5(6) to 5(8) apply to?  Article 11(6)(b) says they "apply to that guidance
-- as they apply to guidance under Article 5(4)", which suggests that without it they would not reach guidance that is not under Article 5(4).
DECLARE `Which guidance Articles 5(6) to 5(8) apply to` IS ONE OF
    `the guidance under Article 5(4), including the guidance on public benefit that Article 7(4) requires it to contain`
    `any guidance that the Commissioner issues or amends`

-- F2.13.  Articles 7(1) and 5(5) name the persons they bind, and a member of the Commissioner's staff is not among them; Schedule 1 paragraph 4(3) says that any function of the
-- Commissioner may, to the extent authorized by the Commissioner, be exercised on the Commissioner's behalf by a member of the Commissioner's staff.
DECLARE `Whether a member of the Commissioner's staff exercising the Commissioner's function is bound as the Commissioner is` IS ONE OF
    `a member of staff exercising a function of the Commissioner under Schedule 1 paragraph 4(3) is bound as the Commissioner is`
    `only the persons that Article 7(1) and Article 5(5) name are bound`

-- The one record of forks of the group.  Each field is a fork point; TYPICALLY names the reading the group takes (FRAGMENT-G2.md, section 2, says why).
DECLARE `Interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
    HAS `how the purposes of an entity are tested` IS A `How the purposes of an entity are tested in Article 5(1)(a)`
            TYPICALLY `at least one charitable purpose is required, and an ancillary purpose counts only beside one`
        `how acting in that capacity qualifies the persons named in Article 5(2)` IS A `How "acting in that capacity" qualifies the persons named in Article 5(2)`
            TYPICALLY `the person must be permitted to act as a Minister, a member of the States Assembly or an equivalent`
        `what a Minister means in Article 5(2)(a)` IS A `What "a Minister" means in Article 5(2)(a)`
            TYPICALLY `any Minister of the Government of Jersey`
        `how a standard of promptness is measured` IS A `How a standard of promptness in Articles 5(7) and 5(8) is measured`
            TYPICALLY `by an input judgement that the time taken was reasonable or practicable`
        `which head a philosophical belief falls within` IS A `Which head a purpose of advancing a philosophical belief falls within`
            TYPICALLY `paragraph (1)(p), by the analogy that Article 6(2)(f) states`
        `how the days of a measured period are counted` IS A `How the days of a period measured from an event are counted`
            TYPICALLY `the day of the event is not counted, so the day after it is the first day`
        `how before issuing or amending guidance is read` IS A `How "before issuing or amending guidance" in Article 5(6) is read`
            TYPICALLY `the consultation and the report must fall on an earlier day than the day the guidance is issued or amended`
        `whether the examples in Article 4(3) add to Article 4(2)` IS A `Whether the examples in Article 4(3) add to Article 4(2)`
            TYPICALLY `the examples illustrate Article 4(2) and are bound by its conditions`
        `how so far as reasonably practicable qualifies Article 4(4)` IS A `How "so far as reasonably practicable" qualifies the standard of conduct in Article 4(4)`
            TYPICALLY `each limb binds so far as it appeared reasonably practicable`
        `what follows from a determination made in breach of the duties on its maker` IS A `What follows from a determination of public benefit made in breach of the duties on its maker`
            TYPICALLY `the determination does not answer the question`
        `how equality and diversity is read` IS A `How "equality and diversity" in Article 6(1)(l) is read`
            TYPICALLY `a purpose must promote both equality and diversity`
        `which guidance Articles 5(6) to 5(8) apply to` IS A `Which guidance Articles 5(6) to 5(8) apply to`
            TYPICALLY `the guidance under Article 5(4), including the guidance on public benefit that Article 7(4) requires it to contain`
        `whether the Commissioner's staff exercising the Commissioner's function are bound` IS A `Whether a member of the Commissioner's staff exercising the Commissioner's function is bound as the Commissioner is`
            TYPICALLY `a member of staff exercising a function of the Commissioner under Schedule 1 paragraph 4(3) is bound as the Commissioner is`
